lped more than one million families around the world navigate baby and toddler sleep. From newborn sleep and changing nap needs to regressions, night waking, early rising, nap transitions and toddler sleep, Little Ones is there as your baby grows. No more wondering when the next nap should be, how long your baby should sleep, or what today’s unexpected nap means for the rest of the day. Open Little Ones. Know what’s next. Terms and Conditions: https://www.littleones.co/pages/terms-and-conditions Privacy Policy: https://www.littleones.co/pages/privacy-policy Email: app@littleones.co\n\nRatings & Reviews\n\n  * 3.3\n\nout of 5\n\n158 Ratings\n\n  * ### Game changer\n\n    1.     2.     3.     4.     5. 2d ago\n\nLsys3\n\nThis app helped us for all 3 kids. Kids were sleeping through the night (waking to eat) right away. The app helps to teach them to self soothe without letting them CIO. They are 2-7YO now and all sleep the whole night in their own beds. I continuously recommend this app to all of my pregnant friends.\n\nOur consultants personalise advice based on the information shared, and the more closely a family is following the schedule framework, the more specific that guidance can often be. We’re grateful for your recommendation and for sharing Little Ones with so many other families.\n\n  * ### Dishonest\n\n    1.     2.     3.     4.     5. 5d ago\n\nRogue.Ravenclaw\n\nI’ve had the app for over a month now and I realized how unfair they’ve been. They had a promotion going on when I purchased this app initially: get 1 month of free help from a professional sleep consultant via chat. So I paid for the app itself and contacted the consultant. She was mildly helpful in the beginning after I explained my baby’s sleep habits in detail. However, she would take “breaks” and be unreachable for a week, sometimes longer, at a time. It gave me the option to swap consultants, but why would I want to have to go through our history again and deal with a new person? I chose to continue working with her, especially when I thought this is like any other profession, and surely she’ll be available more once her first, or second, break finish. She really wasn’t. When she was available, her hours didn’t always align with mine, so we’d send messages in the chat that may sit there unread for hours at a time. Ultimately, she’d give very minimal advice, tell me to work at that for several days and update her later, and then tell me not to rush things when I’d inquire about what the next step would be. I wasn’t asking to do it, I just wanted an idea of what would happen next. They just dragged out the month to not really help, and now, that consultant fee is $19 a month on top of the $15 a month app fee. That’s not a lot to a lot of people, but it is significant to me. Also, how should I expect it to be any more helpful after paying for that? I gave it 2 stars, because the app is useful on its own, but I used to keep track of everything in my notes app. It’s practically the same thing: keeping times of feeds and sleep, and a running log of diapers.\n\n\n8.1.9 Sep 28\n\n  * Minor bug fixes and improvements.\n\n8.1.8 Sep 18\n\n  * Minor bug fixes and improvements.\n\n8.1.7 Sep 16\n\n  * Minor bug fixes and improvements.\n\n8.1.5 Sep 13\n\n  * Minor bug fixes and improvements.\n\n8.1.4 Sep 10\n\n  * Minor bug fixes and improvements.\n\n8.1.3 Sep 9\n\n  * Minor bug fixes and improvements.\n\n7.7.1 Jun 5\n\n  * Minor bug fixes and improvements.\n\n7.7.0 Apr 24\n\n  * Minor bug fixes and improvements.\n\n7.6.9 Apr 16\n\n  * Minor bug fixes and improvements.\n\n7.6.8 Mar 2\n\n  * Minor bug fixes and improvements.\n\n7.6.7 Feb 26\n\n  * Minor bug fixes and improvements.\n\n7.6.6 Feb 16\n\n  * Minor bug fixes and improvements.\n\n7.6.5 Feb 3\n\n  * Minor bug fixes and improvements.\n\n7.6.4 12/15/2025\n\n  * Minor bug fixes and improvements.\n\n7.6.3 12/10/2025\n\n  * Minor bug fixes and improvements.\n\n7.6.2 12/03/2025\n\n  * Private chat has been upgra